pe-ingredient\" style=\"list-style-type: none;border-bottom: 1px solid var(--meadow-list-border-color);padding-bottom: 5px;margin-bottom: 5px;\" data-uid=\"-1\"><span class=\"wprm-recipe-ingredient-amount\">1/2</span>&#32;<span class=\"wprm-recipe-ingredient-unit\">each</span>&#32;<span class=\"wprm-recipe-ingredient-name\">cucumber</span>&#32;<span class=\"wprm-recipe-ingredient-notes wprm-recipe-ingredient-notes-faded\">sliced for crunch</span></li><li class=\"wprm-recipe-ingredient\" style=\"list-style-type: none;border-bottom: 1px solid var(--meadow-list-border-color);padding-bottom: 5px;margin-bottom: 5px;\" data-uid=\"-1\"><span class=\"wprm-recipe-ingredient-amount\">2</span>&#32;<span class=\"wprm-recipe-ingredient-unit\">each</span>&#32;<span class=\"wprm-recipe-ingredient-name\">green onions</span>&#32;<span class=\"wprm-recipe-ingredient-notes wprm-recipe-ingredient-notes-faded\">chopped for freshness</span></li><li class=\"wprm-recipe-ingredient\" style=\"list-style-type: none;border-bottom: 1px solid var(--meadow-list-border-color);padding-bottom: 5px;margin-bottom: 5px;\" data-uid=\"-1\"><span class=\"wprm-recipe-ingredient-amount\">1</span>&#32;<span class=\"wprm-recipe-ingredient-unit\">sheet</span>&#32;<span class=\"wprm-recipe-ingredient-name\">nori</span>&#32;<span class=\"wprm-recipe-ingredient-notes wprm-recipe-ingredient-notes-faded\">cut into strips for garnish</span></li><li class=\"wprm-recipe-ingredient\" style=\"list-style-type: none;border-bottom: 1px solid var(--meadow-list-border-color);padding-bottom: 5px;margin-bottom: 5px;\" data-uid=\"-1\"><span class=\"wprm-recipe-ingredient-amount\">1</span>&#32;<span class=\"wprm-recipe-ingredient-unit\">tbsp</span>&#32;<span class=\"wprm-recipe-ingredient-name\">sesame seeds</span>&#32;<span class=\"wprm-recipe-ingredient-notes wprm-recipe-ingredient-notes-faded\">for added texture</span></li><li class=\"wprm-recipe-ingredient\" style=\"list-style-type: none;\" data-uid=\"-1\"><span class=\"wprm-recipe-ingredient-amount\">to taste</span>&#32;<span class=\"wprm-recipe-ingredient-name\">pickled ginger</span>&#32;<span class=\"wprm-recipe-ingredient-notes wprm-recipe-ingredient-notes-faded\">for a zesty kick</span></li></ul></div></div></div>\n      <div id=\"recipe-10276-equipment\" class=\"wprm-recipe-equipment-container wprm-block-text-normal\" data-recipe=\"10276\"><h3 class=\"wprm-recipe-header wprm-recipe-equipment-header wprm-block-text-bold wprm-align-left wprm-header-decoration-none\" style=\"\">Equipment</h3><div class=\"wprm-spacer\" style=\"height: 15px;\"></div><div class=\"wprm-internal-container wprm-internal-container-equipment wprm-expandable-container wprm-expandable-expanded\" style=\"\"><div class=\"wprm-internal-container-toggle\"><a role=\"button\" aria-expanded=\"false\" class=\"wprm-expandable-button wprm-expandable-button-show\" aria-label=\"Show Section\"><span class=\"wprm-recipe-icon wprm-collapsible-icon\"><svg xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" width=\"16\" height=\"16\" viewBox=\"0 0 16 16\"><g class=\"nc-icon-wrapper\" stroke-width=\"1\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"#333333\" stroke-miterlimit=\"10\" stroke-linecap=\"round\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\"><polyline points=\"3.5,9.5 8,5 12.5,9.5 \"></polyline></g></svg></span> </a><a role=\"button\" aria-expanded=\"true\" class=\"wprm-expandable-button wprm-expandable-button-hide\" aria-label=\"Hide Section\"><span class=\"wprm-recipe-icon wprm-collapsible-icon\"><svg xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" width=\"16\" height=\"16\" viewBox=\"0 0 16 16\"><g class=\"nc-icon-wrapper\" stroke-width=\"1\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"#333333\" stroke-miterlimit=\"10\" stroke-linecap=\"round\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\"><polyline points=\"3.5,6.5 8,11 12.5,6.5 \"></polyline></g></svg></span> </a></div><ul class=\"wprm-recipe-equipment wprm-recipe-equipment-list\"><li class=\"wprm-recipe-equipment-item\" style=\"list-style-type: none;border-bottom: 1px solid var(--meadow-list-border-color);padding-bottom: 5px;margin-bottom: 5px;\"><div class=\"wprm-recipe-equipment-name\">1 Rice Cooker&#32;<span class=\"wprm-recipe-equipment-notes wprm-recipe-equipment-notes-normal\">For cooking sushi rice.</span></div></li><li class=\"wprm-recipe-equipment-item\" style=\"list-style-type: none;border-bottom: 1px solid var(--meadow-list-border-color);padding-bottom: 5px;margin-bottom: 5px;\"><div class=\"wprm-recipe-equipment-name\">1 Mixing bowl&#32;<span class=\"wprm-recipe-equipment-notes wprm-recipe-equipment-notes-normal\">For marinating tuna.</span></div></li><li class=\"wprm-recipe-equipment-item\" style=\"list-style-type: none;\"><div class=\"wprm-recipe-equipment-name\">1 Serving Bowls&#32;<span class=\"wprm-recipe-equipment-notes wprm-recipe-equipment-notes-normal\">For assembling the poke bowls.</span></div></li></ul></div></div>\n    </div>\n    <div class=\"wprm-layout-column wprm-column-width-50 meadow-main-right\">\n      <div id=\"recipe-10276-instructions\" class=\"wprm-recipe-instructions-container wprm-recipe-10276-instructions-container wprm-block-text-normal\" data-recipe=\"10276\"><h3 class=\"wprm-recipe-header wprm-recipe-instructions-header wprm-block-text-bold wprm-align-left wprm-header-decoration-spacer wprm-header-has-actions\" style=\"\">Method<div class=\"wprm-decoration-spacer\"></div>&nbsp;</h3><div class=\"wprm-spacer\" style=\"height: 15px;\"></div><div class=\"wprm-recipe-instruction-group\"><div class=\"wprm-recipe-group-name wprm-recipe-instruction-group-name wprm-block-text-bold\" style=\"color: #000000;\">Preparation Steps</div><div class=\"wprm-spacer\" style=\"height: 5px;\"></div><ol class=\"wprm-recipe-instructions\"><li id=\"wprm-recipe-10276-step-0-0\" class=\"wprm-recipe-instruction\" style=\"list-style-type: decimal;\"><div class=\"wprm-recipe-instruction-text\" style=\"margin-bottom: 10px;\"><span style=\"display: block;\">Rinse sushi rice under cold water until the water runs clear. This helps remove excess starch for a perfect texture.</span></div></li><li id=\"wprm-recipe-10276-step-0-1\" class=\"wprm-recipe-instruction\" style=\"list-style-type: decimal;\"><div class=\"wprm-recipe-instruction-text\" style=\"margin-bottom: 10px;\"><span style=\"display: block;\">Cook the rice according to package instructions. Once cooked, season it with rice vinegar and let it cool slightly.</span></div></li><li id=\"wprm-recipe-10276-step-0-2\" class=\"wprm-recipe-instruction\" style=\"list-style-type: decimal;\"><div class=\"wprm-recipe-instruction-text\" style=\"margin-bottom: 10px;\"><span style=\"display: block;\">In a bowl, whisk together soy sauce, sesame oil, and honey. Add cubed tuna and toss to coat evenly.</span></div></li><li id=\"wprm-recipe-10276-step-0-3\" class=\"wprm-recipe-instruction\" style=\"list-style-type: decimal;\"><div class=\"wprm-recipe-instruction-text\" style=\"margin-bottom: 10px;\"><span style=\"display: block;\">Divide the sushi rice among serving bowls, creating a cozy base for your toppings.</span></div></li><li id=\"wprm-recipe-10276-step-0-4\" class=\"wprm-recipe-instruction\" style=\"list-style-type: decimal;\"><div class=\"wprm-recipe-instruction-text\" style=\"margin-bottom: 10px;\"><span style=\"display: block;\">Top the rice with marinated tuna, avocado slices, cucumber slices, green onions, and nori strips for a colorful presentation.</span></div></li><li id=\"wprm-recipe-10276-step-0-5\" class=\"wprm-recipe-instruction\" style=\"list-style-type: decimal;\"><div class=\"wprm-recipe-instruction-text\" style=\"margin-bottom: 10px;\"><span style=\"display: block;\">Sprinkle with sesame seeds and garnish with pickled ginger. Serve immediately and enjoy your delicious poke sushi bowl!</span></div></li></ol></div></div>\n      \n      \n      <div id=\"recipe-10276-notes\" class=\"wprm-recipe-notes-container wprm-block-text-normal\"><h3 class=\"wprm-recipe-header wprm-recipe-notes-header wprm-block-text-bold wprm-align-left wprm-header-decoration-none\" style=\"\">Notes</h3><div class=\"wprm-spacer\" style=\"height: 15px;\"></div><div class=\"wprm-recipe-notes\"><table>\n<tr>\n<th>Nutrient</th>\n<th>Amount per Serving</th>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Calories</td>\n<td>450</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Fat</td>\n<td>20g</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Protein</td>\n<td>25g</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Carbohydrates</td>\n<td>50g</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Sugar</td>\n<td>5g</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Sodium</td>\n<td>800mg</td>\n</tr>\n</table></div></div>\n      <div class=\"wprm-spacer\" style=\"height: 40px;\"></div>\n      \n    </div>\n  </div>\n</div></div></div>\n\n\n<h2 class=\"wp-block-heading\" id=\"ingredients\"><strong>Ingredients</strong></h2>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">Get ready to whip up a delicious and colorful poke <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Sushi\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">sushi </a>bowl with these fresh ingredients!</p>\n\n\n\n<figure class=\"wp-block-image aligncenter size-full\"><img decoding=\"async\" width=\"400\" height=\"533\" src=\"/wp-content/uploads/2025/12/Ingredients-for-Poke-Sushi-Bowl.webp\" alt=\"A vibrant arrangement of poke sushi bowl ingredients including sushi rice, tuna, avocado, and garnishes.\" class=\"wp-image-10274\" srcset=\"/wp-content/uploads/2025/12/Ingredients-for-Poke-Sushi-Bowl.webp 400w, /wp-content/uploads/2025/12/Ingredients-for-Poke-Sushi-Bowl-225x300.webp 225w\" sizes=\"(max-width: 400px) 100vw, 400px\" /></figure>\n\n\n\n<ul class=\"wp-block-list\">\n<li><strong>2 cups sushi rice</strong> – the base for your bowl</li>\n\n\n\n<li><strong>8 oz sashimi-grade tuna</strong> – cubed for fresh flavor</li>\n\n\n\n<li><strong>2 tbsp soy sauce</strong> – for that umami taste</li>\n\n\n\n<li><strong>1 tbsp sesame oil</strong> – adds a nutty aroma</li>\n\n\n\n<li><strong>1 tsp rice vinegar</strong> – for a touch of tang</li>\n\n\n\n<li><strong>1 tsp honey</strong> – to balance the flavors</li>\n\n\n\n<li><strong>1 avocado</strong> – sliced for creaminess</li>\n\n\n\n<li><strong>1/2 cucumber</strong> – sliced for crunch</li>\n\n\n\n<li><strong>2 green onions</strong> – chopped for freshness</li>\n\n\n\n<li><strong>1 sheet nori</strong> – cut into strips for garnish</li>\n\n\n\n<li><strong>1 tbsp sesame seeds</strong> – for added texture</li>\n\n\n\n<li><strong>pickled ginger</strong> – to taste, for a zesty kick</li>\n</ul>\n\n\n\n<h2 class=\"wp-block-heading\" id=\"how-to-make-poke-sushi-bowl\"><strong>How to Make Poke Sushi Bowl</strong></h2>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">This delightful poke sushi bowl is not only a feast for the eyes but also a treat for your taste buds! With a preparation time of about 20 minutes, cooking time of 15 minutes for the rice, and a little extra time to let the rice cool, you’ll be enjoying this fresh and vibrant dish in no time!</p>\n\n\n\n<figure class=\"wp-block-image aligncenter size-full\"><img decoding=\"async\" width=\"400\" height=\"533\" src=\"/wp-content/uploads/2025/12/Step-by-Step-Poke-Sushi-Bowl-Preparation.webp\" alt=\"A step-by-step visual guide to making a poke sushi bowl, featuring rinsing rice, cooking rice, marinating tuna, and assembling the bowl with fresh toppings.\" class=\"wp-image-10275\" srcset=\"/wp-content/uploads/2025/12/Step-by-Step-Poke-Sushi-Bowl-Preparation.webp 400w, /wp-content/uploads/2025/12/Step-by-Step-Poke-Sushi-Bowl-Preparation-225x300.webp 225w\" sizes=\"(max-width: 400px) 100vw, 400px\" /></figure>\n\n\n\n<h3 class=\"wp-block-heading\"><strong>Step 1: Rinse the Rice</strong></h3>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">Rinse sushi rice under cold water until the water runs clear. This helps remove excess starch for a perfect texture.</p>\n\n\n\n<h3 class=\"wp-block-heading\"><strong>Step 2: Cook the Rice</strong></h3>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">Cook the rice according to package instructions. Once cooked, season it with rice vinegar and let it cool slightly.</p>\n\n\n\n<h3 class=\"wp-block-heading\"><strong>Step 3: Marinate the Tuna</strong></h3>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">In a bowl, whisk together soy sauce, sesame oil, and honey. Add cubed tuna and toss to coat evenly.</p>\n\n\n\n<h3 class=\"wp-block-heading\"><strong>Step 4: Assemble the Bowls</strong></h3>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">Divide the sushi rice among serving bowls, creating a cozy base for your toppings.</p>\n\n\n\n<h3 class=\"wp-block-heading\"><strong>Step 5: Add Toppings</strong></h3>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">Top the rice with marinated tuna, avocado slices, cucumber slices, green onions, and nori strips for a colorful presentation.</p>\n\n\n\n<h3 class=\"wp-block-heading\"><strong>Step 6: Garnish and Serve</strong></h3>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">Sprinkle with sesame seeds and garnish with pickled ginger. Serve immediately and enjoy your delicious poke sushi bowl!</p>\n\n\n\n<h2 class=\"wp-block-heading\" id=\"recipe-snapshot\"><strong>Recipe Snapshot</strong></h2>\n\n\n\n<figure class=\"wp-block-table\"><table class=\"has-fixed-layout\"><thead><tr><th>Feature</th><th>Details</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Category</td><td>Main Course</td></tr><tr><td>Cuisine</td><td>Japanese</td></tr><tr><td>Prep Time</td><td>20 minutes</td></tr><tr><td>Cook Time</td><td>15 minutes</td></tr><tr><td>Extra Time</td><td>10 minutes (cooling time)</td></tr><tr><td>Total Time</td><td>45 minutes</td></tr><tr><td>Dietary</td><td>High Protein</td></tr><tr><td>Serves</td><td>2</td></tr><tr><td>Best Served</td><td>Fresh and chilled</td></tr></tbody></table></figure>\n\n\n\n<h2 class=\"wp-block-heading\" id=\"pro-tips-for-making-poke-sushi-bowl\"><strong>Pro Tips for Making poke sushi bowl</strong></h2>\n\n\n\n<ul class=\"wp-block-list\">\n<li>Choose sushi-grade tuna for the best flavor and safety.</li>\n\n\n\n<li>Marinate your fish for at least 15 minutes to enhance taste.</li>\n\n\n\n<li>Use short-grain rice for that perfect sticky texture.</li>\n\n\n\n<li>Experiment with toppings like seaweed salad or pickled ginger.</li>\n\n\n\n<li>Keep your ingredients chilled until serving for freshness.</li>\n</ul>\n\n\n\n<h2 class=\"wp-block-heading\" id=\"how-to-serve-this-poke-sushi-bowl\"><strong>How to Serve this poke sushi bowl</strong></h2>\n\n\n\n<ul class=\"wp-block-list\">\n<li>Top with sesame seeds for a nutty crunch.</li>\n\n\n\n<li>Serve with a side of soy sauce or tamari for dipping.</li>\n\n\n\n<li>Add pickled ginger for a zesty kick.</li>\n\n\n\n<li>Pair with a refreshing cucumber salad.</li>\n\n\n\n<li>Include seaweed salad for extra flavor and texture.</li>\n\n\n\n<li>Garnish with microgreens or cilantro for a fresh touch.</li>\n\n\n\n<li>Enjoy with a chilled coconut water for a tropical vibe.</li>\n</ul>\n\n\n\n<h2 class=\"wp-block-heading\" id=\"make-ahead-and-storage\"><strong>Make Ahead and Storage</strong></h2>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">Storing your poke sushi bowl properly ensures it stays fresh and delicious!</p>\n\n\n\n<h3 class=\"wp-block-heading\"><strong>Storing Leftovers</strong></h3>\n\n\n\n<ul class=\"wp-block-list\">\n<li>Transfer leftovers to an airtight container.</li>\n\n\n\n<li>Refrigerate within two hours of preparation.</li>\n\n\n\n<li>Consume within 1-2 days for best quality.</li>\n</ul>\n\n\n\n<h3 class=\"wp-block-heading\"><strong>Freezing</strong></h3>\n\n\n\n<ul class=\"wp-block-list\">\n<li>Assemble the bowl without fresh toppings like avocado.</li>\n\n\n\n<li>Use a freezer-safe container or bag.</li>\n\n\n\n<li>Label with the date and freeze for up to 2 months.</li>\n</ul>\n\n\n\n<h3 class=\"wp-block-heading\"><strong>Reheating</strong></h3>\n\n\n\n<ul class=\"wp-block-list\">\n<li>Thaw in the refrigerator overnight if frozen.</li>\n\n\n\n<li>Reheat rice in the microwave with a splash of water.</li>\n\n\n\n<li>Serve cold or at room temperature for best taste.</li>\n</ul>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">Explore more easy <a href=\"https://www.grandmarecipe.com/category/breakfast/\"><strong>breakfast</strong></a> recipes, quick <a href=\"https://www.grandmarecipe.com/category/lunch/\"><strong>lunch</strong></a> ideas, cozy <a href=\"https://www.grandmarecipe.com/category/dinner/\"><strong>dinner</strong></a> meals, tasty <a href=\"https://www.grandmarecipe.com/category/snacks/\"><strong>snacks</strong></a>, and delightful <a href=\"https://www.grandmarecipe.com/category/dessert/\"><strong>dessert</strong></a>.</p>\n\n\n\n<h2 class=\"wp-block-heading\" id=\"fa-qs\"><strong>FAQs</strong></h2>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">Here’s a helpful FAQ about this recipe:</p>\n\n\n<div id=\"rank-math-faq\" class=\"rank-math-block\">\n<div class=\"rank-math-list \">\n<div id=\"faq-question-1\" class=\"rank-math-list-item\">\n<h3 class=\"rank-math-question \"><strong>1. What is a poke sushi bowl?</strong></h3>\n<div class=\"rank-math-answer \">\n\n<p>A poke sushi bowl is a Hawaiian dish that features diced raw fish, typically tuna or salmon, served over a bed of rice and topped with various fresh ingredients. It&#8217;s a vibrant and customizable meal that combines the flavors of sushi with the freshness of salad, making it a popular choice for a healthy and satisfying meal.</p>\n\n</div>\n</div>\n<div id=\"faq-question-2\" class=\"rank-math-list-item\">\n<h3 class=\"rank-math-question \"><strong>2. What are the traditional ingredients in a poke sushi bowl?</strong></h3>\n<div class=\"rank-math-answer \">\n\n<p>Traditional ingredients in a poke sushi bowl include fresh raw fish (like tuna or salmon), sushi rice, soy sauce, sesame oil, and toppings such as avocado, seaweed, green onions, and sesame seeds. You can also add vegetables like cucumber and radish for extra crunch and flavor.</p>\n\n</div>\n</div>\n<div id=\"faq-question-3\" class=\"rank-math-list-item\">\n<h3 class=\"rank-math-question \"><strong>3. How do I make a poke sushi bowl at home?</strong></h3>\n<div class=\"rank-math-answer \">\n\n<p>To make a poke sushi bowl at home, start by cooking sushi rice and letting it cool. Then, dice fresh fish and marinate it in a mixture of soy sauce and sesame oil. Assemble your bowl by placing the rice at the bottom, adding the marinated fish on top, and finishing with your favorite toppings like avocado, seaweed, and vegetables. Drizzle with additional sauce if desired and enjoy!</p>\n\n</div>\n</div>\n<div id=\"faq-question-4\" class=\"rank-math-list-item\">\n<h3 class=\"rank-math-question \"><strong>4. What are some popular variations and toppings for a poke sushi bowl?</strong></h3>\n<div class=\"rank-math-answer \">\n\n<p>Popular variations of poke sushi bowls include using different types of fish like shrimp or tofu for a vegetarian option. Toppings can vary widely and may include mango, edamame, pickled ginger, or spicy mayo. Feel free to get creative with your ingredients to suit your taste preferences!</p>\n\n</div>\n</div>\n</div>\n</div>\n\n\n<h2 class=\"wp-block-heading\" id=\"final-thoughts\"><strong>Final Thoughts</strong></h2>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">We hope you’re as excited to dive into this easy poke sushi bowl as we are! With fresh tuna, creamy avocado, and vibrant toppings, it’s a delightful dish that’s simple to whip up. So gather your ingredients, channel your inner chef, and enjoy every delicious bite. Happy cooking!</p>\n",
  "ingredients": [
